# This is a byte-exact project (PLAN.md §2.1, §5): the golden corpus under
# core/src/test/resources compares generated output against committed
# `expected.xcstrings`/`expected-error.txt` fixtures byte for byte, and the
# committed catalog format itself (indentation, separators, absent trailing
# newline) is part of the spec, not incidental formatting.
#
# Git's default line-ending normalization is therefore actively hostile here.
# A clone on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every checked-out LF
# to CRLF, which silently corrupts the fixtures and turns every byte-comparison
# test into a false failure that has nothing to do with the change being
# tested. `-text` (not `eol=lf`) is deliberate: the bytes already committed are
# already correct for every fixture in this repo, and `eol=lf` would rewrite
# them on top of what's already right -- the rewrite itself is the hazard
# being prevented, not merely the wrong target for it.
* -text
